.TH "GLESHA-CATALOG" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-catalog \- discover, open, or synchronize backup catalogs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha catalog ACTION [SET] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discover, open, or synchronize backup catalogs.
.PP
sync fetches or synchronizes metadata. unlock opens a cached catalog using its catalog passphrase. resolve handles conflicting metadata. These actions do not restore archive contents.
.PP
With \-\-from or \-\-to, only their combined bucket selection may be accessed.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B sync [SET]
Discover catalogs, or synchronize one set.
.IP
Without SET, download catalog metadata without passphrase prompts. With SET, open the catalog, merge changes, and publish metadata. Sync can write to the selected buckets.
.TP
.B unlock SET
Open a downloaded catalog locally.
.IP
Requires the catalog passphrase. Uses cached metadata and makes no cloud requests. Archive files stay encrypted.
.TP
.B resolve SET
Review or resolve conflicting catalog metadata.
.IP
Omit \-\-keep to review differences. Choose \-\-keep local|remote to resolve references, or \-\-authority REMOTE to select a catalog location. Original histories are preserved.
.TP
.B pull SET
Pull remote metadata into the local catalog.
.TP
.B push SET
Publish pending catalog changes.
.TP
.B reconcile SET
Merge compatible catalog histories.
.TP
.B abandon SET
Discard a pending operation's local work.
.IP
Keeps the current catalog and remote objects. Pending chunk spool files may be removed.
.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-\-all
Alias for bare sync; discover only the allowed buckets.
.TP
.B \-\-keep local|remote
Resolve conflicts using local or remote values.
.TP
.B \-\-authority REMOTE
Select the catalog authority during explicit resolution.
.SS Buckets
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Buckets to discover or access; comma\-separated or repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Additional buckets this command may access.
.SS Passphrases
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE|\-
Catalog passphrase file; '\-' reads stdin.
.SS Confirmations
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts for this command.
.SS Global options
.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
Result format: plain or json; status also supports table and csv (default: plain).
.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
Progress on stderr: auto, plain, or off (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
TOML settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
Local state directory; overrides catalog.directory.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Load credentials; existing process variables take priority.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Color mode: auto, yes, or no (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Diagnostic verbosity: debug, info, warn, error, or silent (default: info).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show this command's help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha catalog sync \-\-from b2
glesha catalog unlock SET
glesha catalog sync SET
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Results and tables go to stdout. Activity, prompts, warnings, and errors go to stderr.
Use \-\-format=json for result records, one per line.
Catalog sync records use output version 3; other catalog results retain version 2.
JSON diagnostics and progress use separate version 1 records on stderr; neither stream contains ANSI controls.
Use \-\-progress=off to disable progress. In plain output, redirected stderr or TERM=dumb uses step lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
